---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const LAST_UPDATED = 'October 2026';
const link = 'text-(--forest-light) underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-(--forest)';
---

<Base title="DMCA Policy" description="How to report copyright infringement on CityServ and how counter-notices work.">
  <div class="bg-(--cream) min-h-screen py-12 px-4">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="mb-10">
        <nav class="text-xs text-(--text-muted) mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-(--forest) transition-colors">Home</a>
          <span class="mx-1.5 opacity-40" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
          <span class="text-(--forest)">DMCA Policy</span>
        </nav>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-(--forest)">DMCA Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-(--text-muted)">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
          CityServ respects copyright. If you believe content on cityserv.org infringes a copyright you own, you can ask us to remove it under the Digital Millennium Copyright Act, 17 U.S.C. § 512.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-(--border) bg-white p-8 shadow-[var(--shadow)] space-y-8">
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--forest) mb-3">1. Designated Agent</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed">
            Send copyright notices to our designated agent:
          </p>
          <dl class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm">
            <dt class="font-medium text-(--forest)">Name</dt><dd class="text-(--text-muted)">CityServ DMCA Agent</dd>
            <dt class="font-medium text-(--forest)">Email</dt><dd><a href="mailto:takedown@cityserv.org" class={link}>takedown@cityserv.org</a></dd>
            <dt class="font-medium text-(--forest)">Online</dt><dd><a href="/contact?type=takedown" class={link}>Takedown request form</a></dd>
          </dl>
          <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-(--text-muted)">
            Our agent registration with the U.S. Copyright Office is in progress; the full mailing address will be listed here once it is complete.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr class="border-(--border)" />

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--forest) mb-3">2. What a Notice Must Include</h2>
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed">
            <li>Your physical or electronic signature.</li>
            <li>Identification of the copyrighted work you believe was infringed.</li>
            <li>Identification of the material to be removed, with enough detail for us to find it (a URL is best).</li>
            <li>Your name, mailing address, phone number and email.</li>
            <li>A statement that you have a good-faith belief the use is not authorized by the owner, its agent, or the law.</li>
            <li>A statement, under penalty of perjury, that the information is accurate and that you are the owner or authorized to act for the owner.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed">
            Incomplete notices may not be actionable. Knowingly false claims can create liability under 17 U.S.C. § 512(f).
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr class="border-(--border)" />

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--forest) mb-3">3. What Happens Next</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed">
            When we receive a complete notice we remove or disable access to the material, notify the person who posted it, and log the action. We do not edit user content; it is either removed in full or left up.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr class="border-(--border)" />

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--forest) mb-3">4. Counter-Notices</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed">
            If your content was removed and you believe it was a mistake or misidentification, send a counter-notice to the same address. It must include your signature; identification of the removed material and where it appeared; a statement under penalty of perjury that you have a good-faith belief it was removed by mistake or misidentification; your name, address and phone number; and your consent to the jurisdiction of the U.S. District Court for the Southern District of New York. Unless the original complainant tells us they have filed a court action, we may restore the material 10–14 business days after receiving a valid counter-notice.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr class="border-(--border)" />

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--forest) mb-3">5. Repeat Infringers</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed">
            We terminate the accounts of users who are found to be repeat infringers.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr class="border-(--border)" />

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-(--forest) mb-3">6. Other Content Concerns</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-(--text-muted) leading-relaxed">
            For defamation, harassment, exposed personal information or inaccurate organization details, use the <a href="/contact?type=takedown" class={link}>takedown form</a> and pick the matching reason. See also our <a href="/terms" class={link}>Terms</a> and <a href="/privacy" class={link}>Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
